# Check everything out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# GitHub's windows-latest image ships core.autocrlf=true in the system
# gitconfig, and actions/checkout does not override it. Without this file
# every .go file lands CRLF on a Windows runner, which `gofmt -l .` then
# reports as unformatted — all of them. The build, vet and tests still pass;
# only the formatting gate fails, and it fails 100% of the time.
#
# The .sh entry matters for a different reason: a CRLF `#!/bin/sh` shebang
# is unexecutable ("cannot execute: required file not found", exit 127), so
# go/check_diff_coverage.sh would not run at all.
#
# The .json entry keeps the committed parity corpora byte-stable, so the
# regenerate-and-diff freshness gate compares like with like.
*.go   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Fuzz corpora are byte-exact inputs reproducing a specific failure, so they
# are excluded from normalisation entirely rather than trusted to contain no
# bytes worth preserving. (Every tracked file is pure LF with no NUL today —
# checked — so this file changes nothing on checkout; it exists to keep that
# true on a platform whose git is configured to rewrite line endings.)
go/testdata/fuzz/**  -text
